s/Anchen0823/zeta9-research-notes/zipball/research-2026-10-02","body":"Research notes and reproducible finite certificates for the existing\n[ζ(9) weighted-lattice mission](https://prove2.me/missions/Irrationality_of_%CE%B6%289%29%3A_weighted_lattice_route).\n\n**The irrationality goal remains unproved.** This archive contains written mathematical results,\nindependent reviews and bounded exact/Arb verification. Recent research has not been checked in Lean.\n\nStart with `PACKAGE-README.md`, then `missions/zeta9/README.md` and `PUBLIC_OVERVIEW.md` in the ZIP.\n`source-manifest.json` records every included file's SHA-256 and package boundaries.\n`reproduction-report.json` records the independent extracted-package replay of the latest five groups.\n\nCurrent contributions include a new Gram gcd divisor, exact least-denominator same-side projections,\nan exponential error squeeze for a growing-dimensional positive linear family, a complete scalar\ndispersed-pole classification, and an isolated rational sum with an exact endpoint-leakage repair.\nEach note states its unresolved infinite input; finite small values are not presented as a proof.\n\nThe release uses the task's existing public research repository. It does not replace or rewrite its\nprevious source tree. The package preserves original research paths and certificate bytes, contains\nthe actual dependencies needed for replay, and excludes credentials, caches and third-party paper copies.\n"}
